# DS Claude Terminal -- copy to the SD card root as /dsterm.snippets
#
# Optional. Short prompts you do not want to type on a 10x5 touch keyboard.
# They appear in the composer: COMPOSE on the Control screen, then Y. A
# console with no snippet file is not misconfigured; the list is just empty.
# (Snippets can also live on the computer, in
# ~/.config/ds-claude-terminal/snippets, and are sent to the DS when it
# connects -- docs/CUSTOMIZING.md.)
#
# Format: one `label=body` per line, at most 8 lines.
#
#   label  1-15 characters, must be unique, shown in the picker
#   body   up to 255 characters
#
# Escapes in the body: \n newline, \t tab, \\ backslash. Nothing else, and a
# raw control byte is a parse error rather than something smuggled to the PTY.
# Lines starting with # are comments; blank lines are ignored.
#
# Picking a snippet loads it into the composer and shows it on the top screen;
# nothing reaches Claude until you press A. Picking is not sending.
#
# Fill in your own. These are examples -- remove the # to use one:

# review=Review the last commit for bugs and anything that needs a test.
# tests=Run the test suite and fix whatever fails.
# commit=Write a commit message for the staged changes.
